The k192/k194 review (file-sops-wire on 9a9ab53) found max_stanzas is not range-validated in Backend::Age. max_stanzas => 0 or negative refuses every non-empty document; a non-numeric value numifies to 0 with a Perl warning under (@\$age_keys > \$max_stanzas). Direction is fail-closed (over-refuses, never under-refuses) so it is safe, but the message is confusing. Crypt::Age itself croaks if max_stanzas is not a positive integer. Fix: mirror that in decrypt_data_key/can_decrypt -- croak clearly on a non-positive-integer max_stanzas. Keep the default 64 and the behaviour for valid values unchanged. Add a regression test (extend t/84).

Implemented: _check_max_stanzas validates a positive integer (mirrors Crypt::Age) in decrypt_data_key (ahead of count guard) and can_decrypt (ahead of eval, so it is not swallowed into false). Default 64 unchanged. Regression in t/84. Full suite + interop green (sops 3.13.3, 1466 tests). Not committed; orchestrator to review/commit.

